<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia Ecopetrol sees 36 pct rise in oil exports.</title>
<headline>Colombia Ecopetrol sees 36 pct rise in oil exports.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia's state-run oil company Ecopetrol said Monday it was looking to increase its oil exports about 36 percent to 200,000 barrels per day (bpd) in 1997 from 147,200 bpd currently.</p>
<p>Ecopetrol also forecast that exports from foreign and domestic private sector oil companies, which operate fields under the terms of an association agreement with Ecopetrol, would increase seven percent to 197,000 bpd this year.</p>
</text>
